{
  "info": {
    "name": "e-commerce API · orders",
    "description": "The order endpoints of the e-commerce learning repo, served by `OrderController` at the `orders` root.\n\n**Before running:** start the API with `pnpm start:dev`, which brings up Postgres, Mongo and Mailpit through Docker Compose and boots Nest on the port in `.env` (3000 by default).\n\n**Where this lives:** the repo's `postman/` directory is the source of truth and `pnpm postman:push` publishes it here. An edit made in the app is overwritten by the next push; change the file instead.\n\n**Variables:** `baseUrl` and `productId` come from the shared **e-commerce (local)** environment; select it, and run Create product in the products collection first. `orderId` and `cancelOrderId` stay collection variables, because nothing outside this collection reads them.\n\n**Auth model:** every route is behind `SessionAuthGuard`; there is no public order endpoint. Run Login in the auth collection first: Postman's cookie jar keeps the `session` cookie and attaches it to every request against the same host. Pay, ship and deliver add `RolesGuard` and want a `seller`; every registration is a `customer`, and the README's UPDATE statement is the only way to promote one. The role is read from the database on each request, so the promotion takes effect without a new login.\n\n**Run order:** `Place order` stores the new id in `orderId`, and the next five requests read it: list, get, then pay, ship and deliver in that order, since each transition only accepts the state before it. `Place order to cancel` stores a second id in `cancelOrderId` for `Cancel order`, which would answer 409 on the delivered one.\n\n**Status codes:** 400 comes from the validation pipe or a malformed `Idempotency-Key` and carries no `code`; 422, 404, 409 and 403 come from the typed exception filters and carry a stable `code`. A stock shortfall is a 409 whose body also carries `details`, one entry per short line.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Failure paths",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "401 · POST with no cookie",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{cookielessBaseUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{cookielessBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Sent to `{{cookielessBaseUrl}}`, the same server under a host name the cookie jar holds nothing for, so the guard sees no session whatever is logged in."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "400 · POST without a shipping address",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "The validation pipe rejects the missing object; no `code`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "400 · POST with a malformed Idempotency-Key",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "not-a-uuid"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "The header must be a UUID when present. Nest's own 400 body, no `code`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "422 · POST with a zero quantity",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "`@IsInt()` lets 0 through; the domain's 1 to 999 rule answers `ORDER_QUANTITY_INVALID`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "409 · POST more than the stock holds",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 999\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "`ORDER_STOCK_UNAVAILABLE`, with a `details` array naming the product, the reason and the quantity available. Nothing is allocated: the whole placement rolls back."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('names the short product in details', () => {",
                  "  const details = pm.response.json().details;",
                  "  pm.expect(details).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(details[0].reason).to.eql('insufficient');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "403 · POST pay as a customer",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{orderId}}",
                "pay"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Precondition: the session belongs to a `customer`, the role every registration gets. `AUTH_ROLE_FORBIDDEN`. After the README's promotion statement this answers 204 instead, since the role is read from the database on every request."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "404 · GET an unknown id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000aa",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000aa"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`ORDER_NOT_FOUND`. Another customer's order answers the same 404, so an id leaks nothing."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "400 · GET a malformed id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/not-a-uuid",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "not-a-uuid"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The param DTO rejects it before any query runs."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "422 · GET the list with an unknown status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders?status=refunded",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "refunded"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "`status` is any string at the edge; `OrderStatus` owns the closed set and answers `ORDER_STATUS_INVALID`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "409 · POST ship a cancelled order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/ship",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{cancelOrderId}}",
                "ship"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Precondition: a seller session and `cancelOrderId` set by Place order to cancel, then Cancel order. `ORDER_TRANSITION_ILLEGAL`: cancelled is terminal."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Every request in this folder is named for the status it should",
              "// return, so one assertion here covers all of them and cannot drift",
              "// from the names the way a copy per request would.",
              "const expected = Number(pm.info.requestName.match(/^(\\d{3})/)[1]);",
              "",
              "pm.test(`${expected}`, () => pm.response.to.have.status(expected));",
              "",
              "// 400 comes from the validation pipe and carries no `code`; the typed",
              "// exception filters all do. 202 has no body at all.",
              "if (![202, 400].includes(expected)) {",
              "  pm.test('carries a stable code', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.be.a('string'));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Place order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Idempotency-Key",
            "value": "{{$guid}}",
            "description": "Optional. A UUID; replaying it answers the first order again."
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "Places one line of `{{productId}}`, which Create product in the products collection set. Stock is allocated inside the same transaction; the response carries only the id, the detail is one GET away. `country` is ISO 3166-1 alpha-2; `line2` and `region` are optional."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "",
              "pm.test('Location header points at the new order', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('/orders/' + body.id);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('orderId', body.id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List orders",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders?limit=20&offset=0",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "20",
              "description": "1 to 100. Defaults to 20."
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Zero or greater. Defaults to 0."
            },
            {
              "key": "status",
              "value": "placed",
              "description": "One of placed, paid, shipped, delivered, cancelled.",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "customerId",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Staff only; a customer sending one is scoped to their own orders regardless.",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "A customer sees only their own orders, newest first; a seller sees every order and may filter by `customerId`. Scope comes from the session's role, not from a parameter."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "pm.test('includes the order just placed', () => {",
              "  const ids = pm.response.json().items.map((item) => item.id);",
              "  pm.expect(ids).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId'));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get order",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders",
            "{{orderId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The detail: number, status, decimal amounts, the lines with the product name and price as they were at placement, and the address. Another customer's order answers 404, not 403."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "pm.test('is the order just placed, still placed', () => {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(body.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orderId'));",
              "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('placed');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pay order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/pay",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders",
            "{{orderId}}",
            "pay"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Staff only: `RolesGuard` wants a `seller`. Promote the account with the README's UPDATE statement first; the role is read from the database on every request, so no new login is needed. placed → paid."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Ship order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ship",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders",
            "{{orderId}}",
            "ship"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Staff only. paid → shipped."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Deliver order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/deliver",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders",
            "{{orderId}}",
            "deliver"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Staff only. shipped → delivered, the terminal state."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Place order to cancel",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"lines\": [\n    {\n      \"productId\": \"{{productId}}\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"shippingAddress\": {\n    \"recipientName\": \"Bob Mensah\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Analytical Way\",\n    \"city\": \"London\",\n    \"postalCode\": \"N1 1AA\",\n    \"country\": \"GB\"\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "A second order, so Cancel order has one that is still placed."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('cancelOrderId', pm.response.json().id);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cancel order",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/orders/{{cancelOrderId}}/cancel",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "orders",
            "{{cancelOrderId}}",
            "cancel"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The owner or a seller may cancel while the order is placed or paid; the allocated stock is released in the same transaction. Shipped and later answer 409."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically by Place order. List, Get, Pay, Ship, Deliver and one failure path read it."
    },
    {
      "key": "cancelOrderId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set automatically by Place order to cancel. Cancel order and one failure path read it."
    }
  ]
}
